Whisper: label who put text on the clipboard, for ClickFix protection

What: carries a one-byte "who wrote this" label (mozilla::ClipguardSource) from the
content process to the parent, on nsITransferable and as a field of IPCTransferable (not
as a clipboard flavor, so it never reaches the native clipboard). nsCopySupport sets it:
the person's own Ctrl+C, a page copy/cut handler that replaced the data, or a script's
execCommand (including copying a hidden textarea). A one-line Document getter exposes
whether a page script's execCommand is running.
Why: the parent must tell the person's own copy (never blocked) from a script's write.
An unlabelled content write (for example navigator.clipboard) stays unlabelled and is
treated as a script, which is the safe default.
---
--- a/dom/base/Document.h
+++ b/dom/base/Document.h
@@ -4087,6 +4087,11 @@
